+# Atomic affine RAY and XLINE transforms
+
+This task is stacked on the cached-direction correction in PR111, commit
+`090d345db23094201a1bca07b0af88453b0320e1`, tree
+`f3f7f691479d7d20b83eeae7e45ea3fda4fecc02`. The separate LINE, planar and clone
+PRs are not folded into this task; the JavaScript port is unchanged.
+
+## Corrected behavior
+
+The previous RAY/XLINE implementation wrote the transformed origin before
+validating its direction and normal. A later failure could leave partially
+changed geometry. A collapsed direction silently fell back to its old value,
+projective Matrix4 input lost its bottom row, and changed geometry retained stale
+proxy graphics. Intermediate floating-point overflow and premature rounding also
+lost representable finite results.
+
+`TransformBy(Matrix3, Vector3)` now prepares all three stored vectors before
+publishing anything. `TransformBy(Matrix4)` first checks all sixteen components
+and requires the exact affine bottom row `(0, 0, 0, 1)`.
+
+- The origin is transformed as a WCS point. The direction is transformed as a
+  WCS vector and normalized; translation never affects the direction.
+- Reflections preserve the transformed traversal direction. Singular matrices
+  are allowed when the infinite entity's direction remains nonzero. A zero
+  direction image rejects instead of fabricating the old infinite line.
+- All source components, matrix entries, translation and resulting geometry
+  must be finite. Stored direction and auxiliary normal squared lengths must be
+  within `2e-15` of one, independently of the cached normalized flag.
+- Rejection preserves exact source components, common metadata and proxy bytes.
+  Publication does not invoke user-overridden `Normal` property callbacks.
+- Successful changed geometry clears common proxy graphics. Identity and
+  numerically unchanged results preserve original vectors and proxies. Equality
+  for this no-change decision treats positive and negative zero as equal.
+
+The inherited `Normal` is auxiliary model state, not an inferred RAY/XLINE plane
+normal. Its existing direction-transform convention is retained, with stable
+normalization and retention of the old auxiliary normal when its image is
+exactly zero. The wire schema does not gain an invented plane-normal field.
+Source validation still occurs before an identity transform can return.
+
+## Exact arithmetic and admission limits
+
+Each affine origin coordinate is evaluated as an exact sum of binary64 products
+and translation, then rounded once to nearest binary64 with ties to even.
+Intermediate products may overflow ordinary floating-point arithmetic while the
+final sum remains representable. The bounded internal dyadic implementation
+retains those cancellations. Its arithmetic follows the earlier LINE task but
+is private here to avoid a dependency on that unmerged task's helper.
+
+Direction dot products also remain exact until their common binary scale is
+chosen. Normalization therefore works when the raw image magnitude is much
+larger or smaller than binary64 can store. The final square root and unit-vector
+components are floating-point approximations, not universally correctly rounded
+normalization. The independent oracle checks four ULP per direction component
+and a `2e-15` squared-unit bound.
+
+A nonzero origin coordinate or normalized direction component that rounds to
+zero rejects. Exact zero cancellation is allowed. Overflow of the final origin
+also rejects. These are deliberate conservative library admission rules, not
+claims that AutoCAD mandates the same exception or rounding policy. A
+homogeneous Matrix4 with `M44 != 1` is rejected rather than implicitly divided
+by its homogeneous scale.
+
+Binary64 inputs bound each dyadic dot to roughly 4,200 integer bits. There is no
+unbounded enumeration, recursion or rational GCD. BigInteger arithmetic and the
+prepared-result object have a performance/allocation cost; this task does not
+claim a speed improvement or large-model performance qualification. Public
+origin setters and general Matrix/Vector APIs retain their existing contracts.
+
+```csharp
+var ray = new netDxf.Entities.Ray(new netDxf.Vector3(1, 2, 3),
+    new netDxf.Vector3(2, -3, 6));
+ray.TransformBy(new netDxf.Matrix3(-1, 0, 0, 0, 2, 0, 0, 0, 3),
+    new netDxf.Vector3(4, 5, 6));
+// Reflection and nonuniform scaling preserve the transformed infinite ray.
+```
+
+## Verification
+
+The final focused module contains **1,349 cases**. The same tests pass
+**105/1,349 with the preceding RAY/XLINE methods and 1,349/1,349 after the fix**.
+The before run still includes the new unused helper, but invokes only the old
+entity transform methods. No existing test or independent gate is disabled.
+The test files have SHA-256:
+
+- `InfiniteLineTransformTests.cs`:
+  `b88e971afafb195779e102445faccfb0b03c74d0aca185813a71571366dfc453`.
+- `InfiniteLineNumericalTests.cs`:
+  `209677ef9e22bdd1d48dc5005befebf0bfe6708bf5f68122260c7679722d1f89`.
+
+The wire corpus repeats **21 independently specified mathematical scenarios**
+across two entity kinds, two transform APIs, six typed profiles and text/binary
+transport, producing **1,008 drawings**. It checks metadata/identity retention,
+proxy handling, round trips, auxiliary normal orientation and finite unit
+results. Rejection tests cover every matrix/translation element with nonfinite
+values, malformed source vectors, finite non-unit/zero source state, projective
+bottom rows, collapse, final overflow/underflow and throwing virtual accessors.
+
+`tools/verify_infinite_line_transforms.py` independently reconstructs the cases.
+It compares origin coordinates with Python Fraction exact arithmetic and unit
+directions with 1,500-digit Decimal square roots. Every selected ordered entity
+packet is checked except the values of the entity/owner handles; their framing
+is checked, and every drawing receives a separate ezdxf graph audit. All
+**39,696** parsed-record corruption controls and two missing/extra inventory
+controls reject through the same positive validator. All drawings have zero
+audit errors and zero repairs.
+
+One additional harness case executes **512 seeded numerical scenarios** across
+both entity kinds and transform APIs, spanning matrix binary exponents -900 to
+900. The independent checker regenerates every input bit pattern, checks exact
+origin components and approximate direction/auxiliary-normal components, and
+rejects **4,608** numerical corruptions. The 512 iterations are not counted as
+512 additional harness cases. The older methods' numerical output is separately
+rejected by the new independent numerical oracle.
+
+Complete-suite and final remote Linux/Windows/netstandard2.0 results are
+recorded separately in the PR, against the exact executed head. A focused pass
+is not substituted for final complete-suite execution.
+
+```sh
+DXF_TEST_FILTER=infinite-affine/ dotnet run --project tests/netDxf.Conformance -c Debug
+python tools/verify_infinite_line_transforms.py artifacts/conformance
+# Full regression and all independently maintained verifiers:
+dotnet run --project tests/netDxf.Conformance -c Release
+python tools/run_independent_verifiers.py artifacts/conformance --jobs 4
+```
+
+The harness also honors `DXF_TEST_ARTIFACTS` for isolated output directories.
+
+## DXF sources and remaining scope
+
+Autodesk documents a WCS origin and a WCS unit direction for both records:
+[RAY](https://help.autodesk.com/cloudhelp/2018/ENU/AutoCAD-DXF/files/GUID-638B9F01-5D86-408E-A2DE-FA5D6ADBD415.htm)
+and [XLINE](https://help.autodesk.com/cloudhelp/2018/ENU/AutoCAD-DXF/files/GUID-55080553-34B6-40AA-9EE2-3F3A3A2A5C0A.htm).
+These references establish the stored geometry model, not this implementation's
+numerical tolerances, admission policy or exception behavior.
+
+Wire tests cover R2000/R2004/R2007/R2010/R2013/R2018. The source corpus is
+synthetic mathematical evidence, not new native producer samples. Native
+AutoCAD open/AUDIT/save/reopen, installed-font/visual qualification, historical
+typed dialects, private FIELD/TABLE/cache regeneration, dependency-complete
+import, general version conversion and other entity methods remain separate
+work. Passing this task does not establish universal DXF or AutoCAD parity.
